Subject: [PATCH] outbound: implement non-destructive ResetSessions across stateful protocols

Problem:
Closing tracked flows in statistic.DefaultManager only tears down upper-level
streams. Outbound protocols that maintain internal HTTP/2, HTTP/3, QUIC, smux,
SSH, TCP keep-alive pools, or persistent L3 sockets remain bound to the previous
default interface's source IP after a Windows default interface switch. Calling
ProxyAdapter.Close() directly is unsafe because upstream Close() implementations
permanently mark clients closed (for example canceled contexts or closed flags),
breaking subsequent dials over the newly active interface.

Solution:
Implement non-destructive ResetSessions() across all remaining stateful and
pooled outbound protocols so stale sockets and pooled sessions are dropped while
keeping adapters ready to rebuild connections lazily on the next dial:
- SingMux: calls mux.Client.Reset() and cascades ResetSessions() to wrapped
  inner adapters.
- gRPC (gun) on Trojan/Vless/Vmess: detaches cached *gun.Transport slices and
  closes them outside locks so getTransport() dials fresh H2 connections.
- xhttp (Vless) and mekya (Vmess): resets ReuseManager entries / pending HTTP
  connections and idle+H2 transports without canceling client lifetime contexts.
- Hysteria2 / Hysteria / ShadowQuic: closes the active QUIC connection (and
  Hysteria2 Realm HTTP transport) without marking the client permanently closed.
- TUIC (v4/v5): adds ForceClose() so PoolClient.ResetSessions() immediately
  closes pooled QUIC clients regardless of OpenStreams() count and clears the
  pool lists, with closed checks in getQuicConn() to avoid dial races.
- TrustTunnel: detaches and closes pooled HTTP/2 / HTTP/3 clients.
- SSH: detaches and closes the shared *ssh.Client under cMutex.
- Snell: adds Reset() to component/pool and generation tracking to snell.Pool /
  PoolConn so idle sockets evict immediately and pre-reset leases close instead
  of returning to the pool.
- Shadowsocks+kcptun: detaches and closes active smux sessions while preserving
  the kcptun client context.
- Sudoku: calls MultiplexDialer.ResetSessions() (aborting in-flight dials and
  closing the active mux client) plus resetHTTPMaskClient().
- Mieru: stops the running mieru client under mutex; ensureClientIsRunning()
  lazily restarts it on the next dial.
- Masque: closes L4Client.clientConn cleanly or cancels the current L3 tunnel
  generation (plus HTTP/2 transport) while preserving ipStack and runCtx.
- OpenVPN: tears down the active ovpn.Client and stack device under a bounded
  lock acquisition while leaving runCtx intact for lazy reconnect.
- WireGuard / AmneziaWG: extends wireguardGoDevice with BindUpdate() so
  ResetSessions() rebinds the UDP socket onto the new default interface.

Autonomous mesh VPN daemons with built-in roaming (Tailscale, EasyTier,
ZeroTier) are intentionally left untouched to avoid disrupting their own peer
discovery and control planes.

Unit tests covering pool reset, stale lease invalidation, transport reuse,
SingMux/autoCloseProxyAdapter cascading, WireGuard BindUpdate, and nil-safety
are included across the modified packages.

